 {"question_index": 6, "question_id": 6624, "category": "health", "k": 3, "gold": "C", "parsed_letter": "C", "correct": true, "full_text": "*   A: Food price control (part of access, but not the full definition).\n    *   B: Preventing terrorism (not the definition).\n    *   C: Availability, utilization, stability, and access (this is the standard FAO definition).\n    *   D: Genetically modified crops (a method to achieve food security, not the definition).\n    *   E: Protection from disasters (part of stability, but not the full definition).\n    *   F: Ensuring everyone's access to food (a part of the definition, but less complete than C).\n    *   G: Ending micronutrient malnutrition (part of utilization, but not the full definition).\n    *   H: System of producing enough food (part of availability, but not the full definition).\n    *   I: Protection of agricultural land (not the definition).\n\n    The Food and Agriculture Organization (FAO) defines food security as: \"Food security exists when all people, at all times, have physical, social, and economic access to sufficient, safe, and nutritious food which meets their dietary needs and food preferences for an active and healthy life.\"\n\n    This definition is broken down into four pillars:\n    1. Availability (Is there enough food?)\n    2. Access (Can people get it?)\n    3. Utilization (Is the food nutritious and safe?)\n    4. Stability (Is the supply consistent over time?)\n\n    Option C lists: \"availability, utilisation, and stability, as well as access.\" This matches the four pillars perfectly.\n\n    *   F: \"ensuring everyone's access to food\" - This is only one pillar (Access).\n    *   H: \"system of producing enough food\" - This is only one pillar (Availability).\n    *   C: \"availability, utilisation, and stability, as well as access\" - This covers all pillars.\n\n    Wait\n"}
